  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="2252dcce-e1e0-4a08-b5c2-468676440321"><problem><para>
      <para>Here is the graph of quadratic function \(f\).</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f6d2f05756f240bf0fbb2729b1726aedba9ccbb7"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Andre uses the expression \((x−5)^2+7\) to define \(f\).</para>
      <para>Noah uses the expression \((x+5)^2−7\) to define \(f\).</para>
      <para>Do you agree with either of them? </para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>No</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is No. The vertex of the graph is (5,-7). The graph of Andre’s function would have a vertex at (5,7), and the graph of Noah’s function would have a vertex at (-5,-7). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
